messages:
maria: Flagging a pattern from support: streaming responses sometimes fail mid-stream and users get a 500 with no partial tokens. Painful for UX and retries. We need consistent error envelope for streaming and chunk failures.
kevin: Can you paste an example payload from the logs?
maria: Logged body was: `{'error': 'internal_error'}` and no indication whether chunk N was flushed. Customer lost a whole response.
li: Streaming is tricky because we flush partial chunks. We should add a distinct error code namespace for stream-level problems, e.g. `streaming.partial_failure` or `streaming.chunk_error`. SDKs can then surface a PartialResponseError that contains the partial text and last_token_index.
faiz: Agreed. Proposal for the envelope for streaming errors:
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "streaming.chunk_error",
    "status": 502,
    "message": "stream terminated early",
    "hint": "Retry can resume from last_token_index if request was idempotent",
    "request_id": "req_02X...",
    "details": { "last_token_index": 124, "partial_text": "...the quick brown" }
  }
}
```
kevin: Nice. SDK mapping idea: PartialResponseError extends RedwoodError and exposes `partialText` and `resumeCursor` (last_token_index). For JS the shape could be:
```js
class PartialResponseError extends RedwoodError {
  constructor(payload){
    super(payload.error.message);
    this.partialText = payload.error.details && payload.error.details.partial_text;
    this.resumeCursor = payload.error.details && payload.error.details.last_token_index;
  }
}
```
This lets apps decide whether to retry or present partial output.
li: Also need to standardize HTTP statuses for streaming: 502 for gateway/runner termination, 504 for upstream timeouts, 503 for temporary capacity (retryable), and 500 only for internal bugs. That helps SDKs pick backoff strategies.
maria: Security note from legal: partial_text must be scrubbed and truncated; never more than 1k chars and sanitize PII. Add `sanitized: true` flag if we applied filters.
faiz: Another edge: when a chunk fails but rejoin is possible, backend could return `resume_supported: true`. SDKs can then automatically attempt a resume flow when the original request is idempotent. Consider header `X-Redwood-Resume-Support: 1`.
kevin: For non-streaming endpoints, we should keep the single-envelope approach but include `retryable` boolean and `retry_after` seconds for 429. For streaming, include `resume_supported` and `last_token_index`.
li: Docs: sample app should show try/catch around streaming iterators. Example pseudo-code for JS async iterator: 
```js
try{
  for await (const chunk of client.streamCompletion(req)){
    render(chunk.text);
  }
}catch(err){
  if(err instanceof PartialResponseError){
    showPartial(err.partialText);
    if(err.resumeCursor && canRetry(req)){
      await client.resumeStream(req, { cursor: err.resumeCursor });
    }
  }else{
    showError(err.message);
  }
}
```
Make sure sample app calls `client.streamCompletion` with idempotent input or stores prompts to allow resume.
maria: Migration strategy: roll out structured streaming errors behind a header `X-Redwood-Error-Format: structured_v2` for 4 weeks, then flip. SDKs should default to legacy parsing until they send the header.
faiz: Telemetry: emit `error.code` and `stream.resume_supported` as metrics so we can quantify how many responses can be resumed versus fully lost.
kevin: SDK API consistency: across languages expose `error.code`, `status`, `hint`, `requestId`, `retryAfter`, `retryable`, `partialText`, `resumeCursor`, and raw body. Provide base class `RedwoodError` and subtypes `PartialResponseError`, `AuthenticationError`, `RateLimitError`, `TransientError`, `PermanentError`, `ValidationError`.
li: Edge case: model-side validation failure during generation (e.g., prompt truncation) should map to `validation.prompt_truncated` with status 400 and details about offending token index. That helps client-side prompt heuristics.
faiz: Ops: backend will add sanitization and size limits to `details` and ensure request_id present for every path. Also add unit tests ensuring streaming middleware populates resume metadata.
maria: deploy-bot: Deploy started for branch `feat/stream-error-envelopes` 145. CI: 3/3 green.
kevin: I'll add JS + Python snippets to devex sample apps demonstrating resume flow and typed exceptions. Will send a PR to sample-apps repo.
li: I'll update the error docs page with the streaming section and the HTTP mapping table.
faiz: I'll own backend ticket #1278 for implementation + tests + telemetry.
maria: Action items summarized:
- faiz: implement structured stream error envelope + sanitization (ticket #1278).
- kevin: SDK exception types + sample resume logic in sample apps.
- li: docs + onboarding snippet for streaming errors.
- maria: add telemetry dashboard for top error codes and resume rate.
Thanks all, this should significantly reduce lost responses for customers and make SDK behavior predictable. :white_check_mark:
